"""Poland part of the per-window backdrop for the June 2026 reports (agent_jun_plfacts1/2 digests; dates = publication).
Strict first-dated-mention placement: the 17 and 24 Jun offers and the 17 Jun additional sale sit in their first dated window."""
from wk_jun_global import AB, US, EZ, UK, GLOB, CZ  # noqa: F401
WK_PL = {
 '01': '29-31 May: May flash CPI fell to 3.1% y/y (-0.3% m/m) vs 3.7% expected, as food dropped 1.0% m/m; economists see core near 3% and less pressure for hikes (Erste: CPI near 3% all year). POLGB yields fell ~20bp along the curve. MoF June plan: switch on 3 Jun, sales on 17 and 24 Jun (PLN 6-12bn each), no T-bills; ~56% of 2026 needs financed; budget accounts >200bn at end-May (Drop). BGK plans an FPC switch on 18 Jun.',
 '02': '1 Jun: Q1 GDP revised to 3.5% y/y (flash 3.4), but consumption (3.3%) and investment (2.4%) missed forecasts; May PMI rose to 49.4 (48.5 expected). MoF offers OK0129, NZ0331, PS0731, DS1034, DS0436 and NZ0936 at the 3 Jun switch, buying back DS0726, PS1026, WZ1126, OK0127, PS0527. PAP survey: hold at 3.75% until Q3 2027. Yields rose on US-Iran setbacks; PKO sees the 10Y below 5.60% by week-end.',
 '03': '2 Jun: The MPC held (ref 3.75%) as expected; the statement notes May CPI eased mainly on food and keeps decisions data-dependent, with risk factors unchanged. Banks keep a no-change base case for 2026; ING: hike pricing cooled to ~+25bp for 2026, PKO: an October hike is still fully priced. EKF consensus: GG deficit 6.9% of GDP in 2026, debt ~70% in 2027. MRPiPS proposes a 3.7% minimum-wage rise. BGK priced EUR 2bn of FPC bonds.',
 '05': '3-4 Jun: Glapinski: lower May CPI cuts hike odds; rates are high enough, no reason to change or discuss them; a hike debate would come only with durably higher oil and the end of fuel support. GS, Noble and Erste read it as dovish; yields fell from the morning. MoF switch (3 Jun, MoF database): PLN 11.63bn sold vs 10.90bn bought back (PS0527 7.42bn). OECD: CPI 3.7% in 2026, no cuts before Q2 2027. EC: leeway for energy spending. 4 Jun holiday.',
 '08': '5-7 Jun: May MPC minutes: the CPI outlook is highly uncertain even short term and hinges on fuel prices and the fuel measures; a further CPI rise was possible; some members flagged wage risks; most backed the hold. Millennium: before Glapinski ~1 hike by year-end and ~2 in 12 months were priced. NBP reserves rose to EUR 255.6bn. POLGB yields rose ~6-12bp on the week (PKO) and edged up on Friday ahead of US payrolls.',
 '09': "8 Jun: Budget accounts reached PLN 208.3bn at end-May; 148.7bn of 2026 redemptions remain. May retail bond sales were 5.40bn. Fitch's forecast round (no rating action): GDP 3.3% in 2026, NBP flat at 3.75% to year-end, one cut in 2027. Yields jumped 10bp+ in the morning on Middle East strain and Fed hike pricing; Millennium: 1-2 NBP hikes still priced by year-end; PKO expects a rebound. Week: PDP (Wed), April C/A (Fri).",
 '10': "9 Jun: MPC's Maslowska (Bloomberg): cuts are now more likely than hikes, conditional on CPI staying below 3.5% and no escalation. The government's 2027 macro path: GDP 3.1%, CPI 2.5%, wages 5.6%; public pay +3%, pensions at least +3.48%. Registered unemployment 5.9% as expected. POLGB yields fell 11-14bp as NBP hike pricing receded (Kurtek). EY: rates unchanged, core 3.0% in 2026.",
 '11': "10 Jun: MPC's Dabrowski: no reason to hike after the CPI fall; room even for cuts if the world calms. PKO cut its 2026 CPI forecast to ~3.0% and sees no hikes; Erste: FRAs 9-12M fell ~20bp on 9 Jun. The 2027 minimum wage was set at PLN 4,950 (+3.0%). PDP debt PLN 2,008.2bn (50.6% of GDP) at end-Q1, EDP 61.6%. Drop: POLSTR SPW PLN 40bn. Windfall-tax bill to the SKRM.",
 '12': "11 Jun: POLGB yields fell again as the market priced fewer NBP hikes (PKO's Adamiak), though large borrowing needs keep yields high; EUR/PLN ~4.256. ECB +25bp as expected. Windfall-tax draft: rate cut to 60% from 75%, 2026 take PLN 3.8bn (from 4.75bn). Motyka: no decision yet on extending CPN. World Bank kept Poland's GDP at 3.1%/2.6%. Funds took in PLN 2.7bn in May (Millennium).",
 '15': '12-14 Jun: April C/A deficit EUR 1.56bn vs ~0.34bn expected (fuel imports; 12M 0.9% of GDP, ING). Dabrowski (Bloomberg): a cut is now more likely than a hike; most MPC members more optimistic on inflation. The fuel VAT cut runs to 30 Jun but the excise cut ends (from 15 Jun); Tusk: CPN to end in summer. BGK: Q3 issuance to prefund 2027 FPC needs (~30% secured). PKO: an Iran deal could take the 10Y to ~5.55%.',
 '16': "15 Jun: May CPI final 3.1% y/y, -0.3% m/m (flash). Budget deficit after May PLN 108.2bn (~40% of the 271.7bn limit). MPC's Kotecki: rate changes unlikely to end-2026, hike appetite lower, too early to signal cuts. Fuel excise back from 15 Jun; VAT 8% and price caps to 30 Jun; Szlapka: gradual exit. SPW rallied on the US-Iran deal: DS0436 5.45% (5.57% Fri).",
 '17': '16 Jun: May core CPI 3.1% y/y (-0.1% m/m; April 3.0%). Government adopted the windfall tax (~PLN 4bn for CPN). Tusk: fuel-VAT decision soon; Motyka: conditions to end price caps met (Brent ~$80). BGK: first FPC switch on 18 Jun (buys FPC0427). NBP FSR: the rising SPW share in bank balance sheets adds geopolitical sensitivity. NIK: MPC 2025 guidance gave limited information. PKO: SPW -5-10bp, 2Y/10Y at mid-April lows; DS0436 5.41%.',
 '18': "17 Jun: MoF sold PLN 12.0bn (offer 7-12bn) at 18.3bn demand, cover 1.52 (3-month high). PS0731 4.44bn at 4.918%, DS0436 2.40bn at 5.416%, OK0129 1.93bn at 4.399%, DS1030 1.09bn at 4.711%. NBP's Sobon: no policy cycle. NIK: the 2025 SRW limit was overstated by PLN 84.5bn; the Fiscal Council wants faster consolidation. ING: MPC more dovish than priced; 10Y ~5.4%, a 3-month low; DS0436 5.40%.",
 '19': "18 Jun: MPC's Duda: stable rates the base case, little room for cuts. May voting record: Tyrowicz's +100bp motion rejected again. GUS: June consumer confidence up (BWUK -9.9); price expectations 20.2 from 24.7. BGK switch: sold FPC 1.35bn, bought back FPC0427 1.44bn. Banks: 2026 needs 58-59% financed; the 17 Jun additional sale added PLN 0.79bn. After the hawkish Fed (dots) SPW rose 5-7bp (PAP); DS0436 5.44%.",
 '22': '19-21 Jun: May industry +4.1% y/y (PAP consensus 2.5%), -0.8% m/m (-2.2%). The Sejm passed the windfall tax (60% rate); it now goes to the Senate. Poland filed its 8th KPO payment request. KSF-M: no regulatory WIBOR replacement needed; no new WIBOR deals from 2027; CCyB 2%. NBP: 12-month FX debt repayments EUR 7.2bn. Economists: the MPC has softened and hikes are off the table. Weekend: US-Iran talks in Switzerland. DS0436 5.44%.',
 '23': '22 Jun: May data below consensus: retail +3.0% y/y (3.8%), wages +5.8% (6.0%), construction +3.9% (4.9%), PPI +2.4% (2.5%); employment -0.9%. State Treasury debt PLN 2,135.6bn (+2.2% m/m). MoF drafts a ban on WIBOR in new consumer loans. Citi: CPI may briefly top 3.5% at end-2026. EUR/PLN above 4.27; DS0436 5.42%.',
 '24': '23 Jun: Farm prices -16.2% y/y. The MNB cut 25bp to 6.00%. PLN weakened for a 5th day (~4.283/EUR, the weakest in the region). PKO: the June MPC trimmed FRA hike pricing and carry. BGK sees the 10Y at 5.30-5.35% this week; Pekao: SPW resilient despite supply. MoF offers PLN 7-12bn on 24 Jun (OK0129, NZ0331, PS0731, DS1035, DS0436, NZ0936; DS1035 replaces DS1030/IZ0836). DS0436 5.41%.',
 '25': '24 Jun: MoF sold PLN 12.0bn (demand 15.4bn, cover 1.28) plus 1.32bn additional: PS0731 4.19bn at 4.911%, NZ0331 2.72bn, OK0129 2.36bn at 4.396%, DS0436 1.92bn at 5.417%, DS1035 0.80bn at 5.334%. MoF: 2026 needs ~62% financed; July retail coupons unchanged. Fitch CEO: public finances are the key rating risk. Unemployment 5.9%; orders +143% (SAFE). NBP survey: CPI 3.0%/2.9%. M3 11.0%. DS0436 5.38%.',
 '26': "25 Jun: the 8th KPO request is worth PLN 33.8bn. The Senate amended the windfall tax (cap on the amount). Brent fell to ~$73 as Hormuz traffic normalised; Millennium: rates -6-11bp despite the auction. PKO's Budzicki: no NBP hikes priced any more, stable rates 2026-27 the base case; Tuesday's flash CPI is seen near target. EUR/PLN ~4.29, a 3-month low for PLN. DS0436 5.33%.",
 '29': '26-28 Jun: GPWB 30 Jun change: OK0129 joins TBSP, 1-3Y, 1-4Y and 1-5Y; OK0127 leaves TBSP. Units rise for DS1033/DS1035/DS1034/DS1030/PS0731/DS0436, PS0527 falls (switch); 1-3Y now 6 bonds, TBSP 19. MoF: May EU funds EUR 1.13bn. Erste: 2027 FRAs within 7bp of spot. PKO: yields >30bp below end-May. SPW kept falling: 10Y ~5.30% (ING), DS0436 5.27%. e-petrol: pump prices rise after June.',
 '30': "29 Jun: EC June ESI 100.6; consumer inflation expectations 20.2. Tyrowicz voted against the MPC's 2025 policy report. NBP: Jan-May bank profit -15.6%. GPWB re-posted the 30 Jun PDF with stats: TBSP YTM 4.56%, mod dur 3.76 (as of 25 Jun). PKO: June CPI ~2.7%, small 2027 cut odds priced; Millennium: room for lower yields exhausted. Due: flash CPI (30 Jun), MoF/BGK Q3 supply (30 Jun), MPC 7-8 Jul. DS0436 5.30%.",
}
